 Removal tooltip (plan §2 #73): each side pane's removal bar (`words.ts` `RemovalPoint`, class `REMOVAL_BAR_CLASS`) carries its removed text, and `eq` compares tone and text; `removalTooltip.ts` opens a `hoverTooltip` (in `document.body`) only while the pointer is on a bar's own box (`:hover` on that class), reads the text from that bar's decoration (`removalAt`), never from `chunk.words`, copies the pane's font, ligatures and code colour from its computed style, and closes when the bar goes; `removalText.ts` holds the pure display rules (the one joining line break left out — on an empty line the trailing one first — whitespace-only text as `·`/`→`/`↵` marks); `theme.css` draws a kept final line break as its empty line (`::after` zero-width space, not copied).
-
-Change marks (plan §2 #80): `Frame` owns `internal/markLanes.ts` (`MarkLanes`), one `.change-marks` lane appended to each pane's `view.dom` over its scrollbar, `hidden` while `MergeOptions.marks`/`showMarks` say no; it repaints from `Frame`'s rows only while shown and dirty (rows or geometry changed, `setDiagnosticsEffect`), never on scroll. A wheel over a lane is forwarded to that pane's `scrollDOM` (the lane is not inside it). `marks.ts` holds the pure rules: places from `tone.ts` `paneTone` (the one tint rule, bands use it too) and from `forEachDiagnostic` on the line block (a problem in collapsed lines sits on its wave line), WebStorm's stripe geometry (14 px lane, 2 px floor, Windows arrows), paint order (errors over changes over warnings over info) and `tickAt` (nearest top within `PICK_DISTANCE_PX`, which the lane hands the CSS hit band as `--mark-pick`). `markJump.ts` acts on a tick's click, positions read at click time; the controller builds it into `Frame`'s `jump` part: a side tick outlines its change through `SideFocus.focusChange`, a Result tick first selects the innermost hidden middle range holding the place, both ends counted (`revealSteps`: `foldField` shows hidden lines holding a non-empty selection, so also an empty line at a range's edge, such as a file's end after its last line break), and then puts the cursor at the place's start; both put the line a third down (`viewport.ts` `thirdScrollTop`).
